# Scrollable Index Content, Not the Whole Page

For index/list-style pages (search results, tables, feeds) rendered inside
`AuthenticatedLayout`'s `<main>` (which is `overflow-auto`), don't let the
entire page grow and scroll. Instead, size the page to the available viewport
and make only the list/results region (and any independent side panel)
scroll within their own bounded containers. Fixed elements like page titles,
toolbars, and filter bars must stay on-screen without needing to scroll past
the list.

## Pattern

1. Root page element: `h-full min-h-0 flex flex-col` (fills the layout's
   `<main>`, which already has a definite height).
2. Headers/toolbars that should stay pinned: `flex-none`.
3. The row containing a side panel + main content: `flex flex-1 min-h-0 gap-*`.
4. Any independently-scrolling region (filter sidebar, results grid): give it
   `min-h-0 overflow-y-auto` (add `flex-1` if it should fill remaining space
   in a flex column).

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - bounded page, independently scrolling panel + results
<div className="flex h-full min-h-0 w-full flex-col">
  <div className="flex-none">{/* title, always visible */}</div>
  <div className="flex min-h-0 flex-1 gap-8">
    <aside className="w-80 shrink-0 overflow-y-auto">{/* filters */}</aside>
    <div className="flex min-h-0 min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col">
      <div className="flex-none">{/* toolbar, always visible */}</div>
      <div className="min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-y-auto">{/* results grid */}</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

// ❌ BAD - unbounded page grows with content, forcing the whole page
// (and the filter bar with it) to scroll to reach items further down
<div className="w-full">
  <div>{/* title */}</div>
  <div className="flex gap-8">
    <aside>{/* filters */}</aside>
    <div>{/* results grid, unbounded height */}</div>
  </div>
</div>
```

See `frontend/src/pages/buy/CarSearch.tsx` for a full example.
